## 4. Saturation pair 1,024 -> 4,096: what the 4,096 side already bounds (i* is non-decreasing; U_L(32K/4K) >= 131,072 > 65,536)
  i*(32K/4K; 65,536) = 1.8865-1.9433 bits/fact = 15.09-15.55 bits/slot (lower bound on the 4,096 side at any U_L >= 65,536 on these draws)
  if i*(32K/4K; U_L) = 1.887: SUBPROPORTIONAL (rho < 3.0) needs i*(8K/1K; U_L) > 2.515 bits/fact (a_use > 0.681; 20.1 bits/slot)
  if i*(32K/4K; U_L) = 2.000: SUBPROPORTIONAL (rho < 3.0) needs i*(8K/1K; U_L) > 2.667 bits/fact (a_use > 0.706; 21.3 bits/slot)
  if i*(32K/4K; U_L) = 2.120: SUBPROPORTIONAL (rho < 3.0) needs i*(8K/1K; U_L) > 2.827 bits/fact (a_use > 0.731; 22.6 bits/slot)
  if i*(32K/4K; U_L) = 2.250: SUBPROPORTIONAL (rho < 3.0) needs i*(8K/1K; U_L) > 3.000 bits/fact (a_use > 0.758; 24.0 bits/slot)
  if i*(32K/4K; U_L) = 2.400: SUBPROPORTIONAL (rho < 3.0) needs i*(8K/1K; U_L) > 3.200 bits/fact (a_use > 0.787; 25.6 bits/slot)
  bits per slot already held at 4,096 slots, load 4: 16.25-16.47 (65,536 updates; load 2 is at the 5-bit ceiling)
  bits per slot already held at 4,096 slots, load 2: 9.91-9.92 (65,536 updates; load 2 is at the 5-bit ceiling)

